\f1\fs32\b The word that makes separation\b0\fs24\par
\f1\fs20 Torah: Genesis 1:1\u8211?6:8 | Haftarah: 1 Samuel 20:18\u8211?42 | Gospel: Matthew 24:29\u8211?36\par
\f0\fs22\i God creates by speaking and separating; the Spirit hovers over the emptiness and the Word calls light and order. Sin is de-creation: the prophets use the image of tohu va-vohu for where sin ends up (though linguistically other words than hevel/riq). Cain grasps and lets sin rule; Jonathan \u8212? \u8220?the LORD has given\u8221? \u8212? receives and gives. Ruling over sin succeeds not from our own emptiness but by the Spirit. And when the lights go out, His word remains: \u8220?heaven and earth shall pass away, my words shall not\u8221? (24:35).\i0\par
\par\f0\fs24 
\par\b\fs28 \u167?0 Observation round\b0\fs24\par


\par\b\fs24 0.1 Blind observation\b0\fs24\par


\par Genesis 1 creates by speaking: \u8220?and God said\u8230? and it was\u8221?; bara is used only for God\u8217?s creating. Light comes on day 1 (1:3), the lights (sun/moon/stars) only on day 4 (1:14-18), set \u8220?for signs and for seasons\u8221? (moadim). Seven times \u8220?it was good\u8221?; man in God\u8217?s image (1:27). Then Genesis 3: \u8220?she took\u8230? and ate\u8221? (grasping, wanting to be as God); the relationship breaks, the ground bears thorns. Genesis 5: eight times \u8220?and he died,\u8221? with Noah (\u8220?rest/comfort\u8221?) as exception. Genesis 6: \u8220?it repented the LORD\u8230? it grieved Him\u8221? (6:6), but \u8220?Noah found grace (chen) in the eyes of the LORD\u8221? (6:8). Haftarah (Machar Chodesh): \u8220?tomorrow is the new moon\u8221?; Jonathan\u8217?s covenant with David across the parting (\u8220?the LORD between us\u8230? for ever\u8221?). Gospel: the lights go out (Matt. 24:29), \u8220?heaven and earth shall pass away, my words shall not\u8221? (24:35), the hour known only to the Father (24:36).\par


\par\b\fs24 0.2 The four axes as an open question\b0\fs24\par


\par Does the weight fall on what God is and does (Source: the creating, remaining word), on the movement through time (Trajectory: beginning \u8594? fall \u8594? death \u8594? grace \u8594? end, and the renewal of the moon), on the wholeness of gift/grasp (Coherence: receiving vs grasping), or on the response (Will: hearing, abiding)?\par


\par\b\fs24 0.3 The centre of gravity read off\b0\fs24\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? Load-bearing are \b Source\b0  and \b Trajectory\b0 : God speaks the world into being (gift), and that same word remains when the creation passes away (Matt. 24:35). Centre of gravity: the word that remains \u8212? from \u8220?in the beginning\u8230? and God said\u8221? to \u8220?my words shall not pass away,\u8221? with the gift of creation, the grasp of the fall, and an ending in grace (6:8).\par


\par\b\fs24 0.4 Framing test\b0\fs24\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8908? Guarded. The weekly reflex (receiving vs grasping) is here not imposed but text-central: creation is the primal gift, the fall the primal grasp (\u8220?she took\u8221?). But the centre does not stay on that axis; the real deepening is the word-as-constant (Trajectory, Matt. 24:35). Guard: John 1:1-3 (the Logos in creation) and Matt. 24 are confessional horizon, not peshat-setter; the \u8220?speaking\u8221? in Genesis 1 is God\u8217?s word, not simply a doctrine of the Trinity.\par



\par\b\fs28 \u167?1 The thread\b0\fs24\par


\par The world exists by a spoken word; it hangs on the Speaker, not on itself. So everything is gift before it is achievement. Man grasps what he was given to receive, and brings in death; God is grieved, and yet grace is found. And when at the end the lights go out and heaven and earth pass away, the word that called them remains.\par



