\par\b\fs28 \u167?4 Sources round\b0\fs24\par


\par Van de Giessen covers Genesis 1\u8211?25; the rabbinic witnesses were verified via Sefaria.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b Van de Giessen (pre-peshat).\b0  Bara (1:1) is used in the Bible only for God\u8217?s creating; cross-refs to John 1:1-3 and Heb. 11:3 (the world by the word). The light of day 1 (1:3) precedes the lights of day 4 \u8212? an old crux he discusses without forcing it. At 1:14 he notes the lights \u8220?for signs and seasons.\u8221? And Noah (6) means \u8220?rest/comfort,\u8221? a counter-note in the register of death.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b Rashi on 1:14.\b0  \u8220?Signs\u8221? points to the renewal of the moon \u8212? the lights govern the appointed times and the new moon. That ties the parashah directly to the Machar Chodesh haftarah.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8223? \b Ibn Ezra on 1:14.\b0  \u8220?Signs\u8221? may also point to hours and to lunar and solar eclipses \u8212? the lights as a measurable order, not as gods. Chizkuni places the lights in the firmament. Illustrative.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8907? \b John 1:1-3 / Matthew 24 (confessional).\b0  The creating word of Genesis 1 is confessed as the Logos who \u8220?in the beginning was with God\u8221? and became flesh; and \u8220?my words shall not pass away\u8221? (24:35) continues the enduring-word motif. Horizon, not peshat-setter.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b De-creation in the prophets.\b0  Jeremiah 4:23 and Isaiah 34:11 use the image of tohu va-vohu for the consequence of sin: the creation order is dismantled, the light taken away; Isaiah 45:18 says the opposite \u8212? God did not create the earth a tohu but to be inhabited. Precision note (set by the author): the \u8220?emptiness of sin\u8221? has its own roots (hevel, shav, awen, riq) and is linguistically not tohu/bohu; the link is thematic/theological, not lexical. Cassuto reads tohu as clay on the potter\u8217?s wheel \u8212? raw, waiting, not moral chaos.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b Genesis 3:16 \u8596? 4:7 (grammatical mirror).\b0  The same syntax with teshuqah (desire) and mashal (rule): to Eve \u8220?he shall rule over you,\u8221? to Cain \u8220?you must rule over it\u8221? (timshal-bo). God reverses the axis: Cain is addressed on his moral sovereignty over the lurking drive. Teshuqah occurs in the whole Tanakh only 3\u215? (Gen. 3:16; 4:7; Song 7:10).\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222?/\u-10179?\u-8223? \b Genesis 4:8 (text-critical gap).\b0  The MT has \u8220?and Cain spoke to his brother Abel\u8221? without the direct speech; SP, LXX, Vulgate, Peshitta and Targum add \u8220?let us go into the field.\u8221? Three readings: scribal omission (homoioteleuton around \u8220?the field\u8221?), harmonisation by the translators, or deliberate aposiopesis \u8212? the omission then stressing that Cain\u8217?s words were mere pretext to lure him away from the witnesses.\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8222? \b Jonathan = \u8220?the LORD has given\u8221? (Yehonathan).\b0  The name lays bare the contrast with Cain: grasping versus gift. Jonathan dismantles his dynastic claim and preserves the anointed (hesed); the empty place at Saul\u8217?s table (1 Sam. 20:18,25) stands against the covenant that remains whole (20:42). Two questions frame the parashah: \u8220?where are you?\u8221? (3:9, the Creator) and \u8220?where is your brother?\u8221? (4:9, the neighbour).\par


\par \u9898? \b Onkelos\b0  on 1:1/1:3: still to be verified.\par


\par \b Revision gate.\b0  Did the round shift the centre? Confirming: bara-as-God\u8217?s-act-alone and \u8220?signs = new moon\u8221? (Rashi) strengthen Source/Trajectory and knot the three readings on one thread \u8212? the word that creates, sets the times, and remains.\par



\par\b\fs28 \u167?5 Direction test as horizon\b0\fs24\par


\par \u-10179?\u-8907? Confessional. The word by which God created \u8220?became flesh and dwelt among us\u8221? in Yeshua (John 1:14) \u8212? here, and only here, accommodation applies. And when in Matthew 24 the fourth-day lights go out, His word remains: whoever abides in it, abides. \u-10179?\u-8908? Guarded: Matt. 24 and John 1 do not settle the peshat of Genesis; \u8220?God said\u8221? is first of all God\u8217?s creating speech.\par



